<title>ISRAEL: Teva Q3 earnings per ADR $0.39.</title>
<headline>Teva Q3 earnings per ADR $0.39.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Teva Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd.</p>
<p>			   (in millions of dollars except EPS)</p>
<p>			   Q3 96	Q3 95	 9-MTH 96   9-MTH 95</p>
<p>Sales		    236.6	201.1	 676.1	581.1</p>
<p>Operating profit	34.6	 26.8	  86.4	 77.9</p>
<p>Net Profit		23.9	 19.6	  58.1	 55.6</p>
<p>Earnings per ADR	0.39	 0.32	  0.95	 0.91</p>
<p>(ADR=10 ordinary shares)</p>
<p>Teva said the 1995 results do not include a one-time pretax charge of $4.7 million for all of 1995 for writing off debt from the Clalit sick fund.</p>
<p>The nine-month 1996 results do not include a one-time pretax charge of $19.8 million taken in the second quarter for Teva's merger with Biocraft.</p>
<p>Lehman Brothers had estimated Teva would report third-quarter earnings per American depositary receipt (ADR) of $0.35.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
